# The generated half of .agent/ must never be merged textually. Git would inject conflict markers
# into graph.json, making it invalid JSON — loadGraph then refuses to overwrite it (correctly),
# and `godkit save` is stuck until someone hand-merges a machine-written node array, which is
# meaningless work. Worse, deleting the file to escape costs a FULL rebuild instead of an
# incremental one.
#
# `-merge` makes git keep our side intact and just flag the conflict, so the file stays valid.
# Resolve by taking either side — both are real graphs — then refreshing:
#   git checkout --ours .agent/graph.json .agent/meta.json .agent/MAP.md
#   godkit scan && ... && godkit save     # only the delta gets re-analyzed
#
# The hand-written half (BOARD.md, THREAD.md, log/, tasks/, skills/) is deliberately NOT listed:
# those hold work a person or agent actually wrote, and a real textual merge is what you want.
.agent/graph.json -merge
.agent/meta.json  -merge
.agent/MAP.md     -merge
